      "problem": "Find the **exact** value of the limit.\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the root rule, we get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to 0}(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({lim}_{x\\to 0}(3{x}^{2}+6x+9))}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3(0)^{2}+6(0)+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0+0+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{9}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{729} \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
